An assignment whose value a larger expression uses
(diag.one_assignment_per_statement, info) and string `-` between two
known strings (diag.prefer_explicit_trim_concat, info); a pure chain and
numeric `-` stay silent (issue #347).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Build;
	:DECLARE nTotal, nCount, sStatus, sDefault, sJoined;
	nTotal := (nCount := 5) * 2;
	sStatus := sDefault := "PENDING";
	sJoined := "Sample   " - "Analysis";
	nTotal := nTotal - 1;
	:RETURN sJoined;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Build;
	:DECLARE nTotal, nCount, sStatus, sDefault, sJoined;

	nTotal := (nCount := 5) * 2;
	sStatus := sDefault := "PENDING";
	sJoined := "Sample   " - "Analysis";
	nTotal := nTotal - 1;

	:RETURN sJoined;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
3:13-3:24 info one_assignment_per_statement: Assignment ':=' is used inside a larger expression - give it a statement of its own
5:25-5:26 info prefer_explicit_trim_concat: String '-' trims trailing spaces from the left operand, then appends the right - write Trim(a) + b to say so (Trim also removes trailing tabs and line breaks, which '-' keeps)
